content:
It seems there was a misunderstanding in the response formatting. The correct approach to announce your bid using the provided tools would be as follows:

```json
{
    "type": "function",
    "function": {
        "name": "announce_bid",
        "description": "Publicly announce the bid you intend to submit in THIS auction. Non-binding; your sealed bid is submitted with submit_bid in the execution phase.",
        "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
                "amount": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "description": "Intended bid (>= 10)."
                },
                "note": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Optional short note shown with the announcement."
                }
            },
            "required": [
                "amount"
            ]
        }
    }
}
```

To correctly announce a bid of 55 credits without a note, the JSON should be:

```json
{
    "type": "function",
    "function": {
        "name": "announce_bid",
        "arguments": {
            "amount": 55
        }
    }
}
```

This JSON properly formats the function call to announce a bid of 55 credits for the auction.

submit_bid {
    "name": "submit_bid",
    "arguments": {
        "bid": 58
    }
}

{
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
    "name": "submit_bid",
    "arguments": {
      "bid": 57
    }
  }
}
